------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY BUNDLED DATA ATTRIBUTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This distribution bundles third-party data whose license requires that its
attribution notice be carried in redistributions. The authoritative, per-file
provenance and conversion record are retained in `models/PROVENANCE.md`.

* PaddleOCR PP-OCR models and recognition dictionaries
  (`models/ppocrv5_det.onnx`,
   `models/ppocrv5_rec.onnx`,
   `models/ppocrv5_cls.onnx`,
   `models/ppocr_keys_v5.txt`,
   `models/ppocrv5_rec_th.onnx`,
   `models/ppocr_keys_th.txt`)
  Copyright (c) PaddlePaddle Authors.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  The bundled files are the PP-OCRv5 mobile text-detection and text-recognition
  models, the PP-LCNet text-line-orientation classification model, the PP-OCRv5
  recognition character dictionary, and the PP-OCRv5 Thai recognition model
  (`th_PP-OCRv5_mobile_rec`) with its Thai recognition dictionary, converted to
  ONNX (via Paddle2ONNX) from the upstream PaddlePaddle weights, then
  post-processed by a deterministic ONNX dim-name/shape-hint cleanup so the
  pure-Rust `tract` runtime can parse them (no weight changes). The ONNX weights
  ship as data files; the default recognition dictionary is embedded into the
  binary via `include_str!`, while the Thai dictionary loads from disk via the
  `OCRSPINE_REC_DICT` override.
  Source: https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR
  Per-file provenance and the conversion record are retained in
  `models/PROVENANCE.md`.

* Noto Sans Thai and Sarabun fonts (test fixtures only)
  (`tests/fixtures/thai/fonts/NotoSansThai-VF.ttf`,
   `tests/fixtures/thai/fonts/Sarabun-Regular.ttf`)
  Noto Sans Thai: Copyright The Noto Project Authors.
  Sarabun: Copyright Cadson Demak Co., Ltd.
  Both licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (the accompanying
  `OFL-NotoSansThai.txt` / `OFL-Sarabun.txt` next to the fonts). Used only to
  render the synthetic Thai OCR test fixtures under `tests/fixtures/thai/`; not
  linked into or shipped with the library.
  Source: https://github.com/google/fonts

